<title>PAKISTAN: KARACHI PORT HANDLES 56,227 TONNES CARGO.</title>
<headline>KARACHI PORT HANDLES 56,227 TONNES CARGO.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 56,227 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 22,075 tonnes on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			  2,991	    6,573</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  53,236	   15,502</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, three ships are expected to sail and three to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Veg Oil		 18,600	 Kristal		14/8</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
